---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import ZoomImage from "../../components/ZoomImage.astro";
import toc from "../../generated-toc.json";
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const sections = toc.examples;
---
<BaseLayout title="Examples">
  <div class="prose-narrow">
    <h1>Examples — towns & counties</h1>
    <p>
      Worked SQL examples on the Pacific Northwest <code>pnw_towns</code>,
      <code>pnw_counties</code>, and <code>fips</code> tables. Each section
      has runnable examples with starter editors — click <strong>Show solution</strong>
      to populate one, then <strong>Run</strong> to see the result. You can
      also try your own version first and use <strong>Check answer</strong>
      to confirm.
    </p>
    <p>
      Every section also has scroll-driven diagrams that show what a command
      does to a table, step by step. The
      <a href={`${base}scrollytelling/`}>scrollytelling gallery</a> lists all of them.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="my-4">
    <ZoomImage
      src={`${base}images/pnw_towns_counties_mermaid.png`}
      alt="ER diagram for the Pacific Northwest towns and counties database — three tables: pnw_towns, pnw_counties, and fips. A full text description is available below the image."
      caption="ER diagram · towns & counties"
    >
      <Fragment slot="description">
        <p>Three tables and two helper views.</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong><code>pnw_towns</code></strong> — one row per town. Columns: <code>town_id</code> (primary key), <code>town</code>, <code>state</code>, <code>primary_county</code>, <code>secondary_county</code>, <code>tertiary_county</code>, <code>primary_county_id</code>, <code>secondary_county_id</code>, <code>tertiary_county_id</code> (foreign keys), <code>population_2020_census</code>, <code>population_2010_census</code>, <code>land_area_sq_mi</code>.</li>
          <li><strong><code>pnw_counties</code></strong> — one row per county. Columns: <code>county_id</code> (primary key), <code>county</code>, <code>state</code>, <code>fips_short</code>, <code>county_seat</code>, <code>county_seat_town_id</code> (foreign key; <code>NULL</code> if the seat is not in <code>pnw_towns</code>), <code>year_established</code>, <code>origin</code>, <code>etymology</code>, <code>population_2022</code>, <code>land_area_sq_mi</code>.</li>
          <li><strong><code>fips</code></strong> — FIPS codes for every US state and county (3,195 rows). Columns: <code>fips</code> (state code × 1000 + county code, so 41001 is Baker County, Oregon), <code>name</code> (<code>OREGON</code>, <code>Baker County</code>), <code>state</code> (the abbreviation, such as <code>OR</code>; blank on the state rows).</li>
        </ul>
        <p><strong>Relationships:</strong> a town's <code>primary_county_id</code> (and optionally <code>secondary_county_id</code>/<code>tertiary_county_id</code>) matches a <code>county_id</code> in <code>pnw_counties</code>; the name columns (<code>primary_county</code> and so on) hold the same county by name. A county's <code>county_seat_town_id</code> matches a <code>town_id</code> in <code>pnw_towns</code>. <code>fips</code> has no key column linking it to the other two tables: its <code>state</code> holds abbreviations (<code>OR</code>) where theirs holds full names (<code>Oregon</code>), so the diagram shows it on its own. A county matches its FIPS row when <code>fips</code> equals the state code times 1000 plus <code>fips_short</code>.</p>
        <p><strong>Helper views:</strong> <code>towns_with_county</code> and <code>towns_with_counties</code> both project <code>(town, primary_county)</code> from <code>pnw_towns</code>.</p>
      </Fragment>
    </ZoomImage>
  </div>

  <ul class="not-prose list-none grid gap-3 my-8 p-0">
    {sections.map((s, i) => (
      <li class="list-none">
        <a
          href={`${base}examples/${s.slug}`}
          data-toc-link
          data-checkable-ids={s.checkableIds.join(",")}
          class="flex items-center justify-between gap-3 rounded-xl border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 p-4 no-underline hover:border-brand-500 transition"
        >
          <span class="flex items-baseline gap-3 min-w-0">
            <span class="text-slate-400 dark:text-slate-500 font-mono text-sm w-6 text-right flex-shrink-0">{i + 1}.</span>
            <span class="font-semibold truncate">{s.title}</span>
          </span>
          <span class="flex items-center gap-2 flex-shrink-0 text-sm">
            <span class="text-slate-400" data-section-progress>{s.checkableIds.length ? `0/${s.checkableIds.length}` : ""}</span>
            <span class="hidden text-emerald-600 dark:text-emerald-400" data-section-complete>✓ Complete</span>
          </span>
        </a>
      </li>
    ))}
  </ul>

  <script>
    import { refreshSidebarProgress } from "../../lib/sidebar";
    refreshSidebarProgress();
    window.addEventListener("sqlt:progress-changed", refreshSidebarProgress);
  </script>
</BaseLayout>
